<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_165259> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "HD 165259, also known as HR 6751 is a triple star system located in the southern circumpolar constellation of Apus. It has an apparent magnitude of 5.86, making it faintly visible to the naked eye Parallax measurements place the system at a distance of 138 light years, and it is currently receding with a heliocentric radial velocity of 13.1 km/s."@en .
