<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Timekeeping_on_Mars> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Though no standard exists, numerous calendars and other timekeeping approaches have been proposed for the planet Mars. The most commonly seen in the scientific literature denotes the time of year as the number of degrees from the northern vernal equinox, and increasingly there is use of numbering the Martian years beginning at the equinox that occurred April 11, 1955."@en .
