<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Upsilon_Andromedae_e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Upsilon Andromedae e** is the proposed outermost [extrasolar planet](:Extrasolar_planet) orbiting the star [Upsilon Andromedae](:Upsilon_Andromedae) in the [constellation](:Constellation) of [Andromeda](:Andromeda_%28constellation%29). If it exists, this planet would be one of the most [Jupiter](:Jupiter)-like exoplanets found in terms of mass and [semi-major axis](:Semi-major_axis). However, subsequent studies have found that the apparent planetary signal is more likely to be an instrumental artifact."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
