<http://dbpedia.org/resource/51824_Mikeanderson> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "51824 Mikeanderson, provisional designation 2001 OE30, is an Eoan asteroid in the outer region of the asteroid belt, approximately 5 kilometers in diameter. It was discovered on 19 July 2001, by astronomers of the Near-Earth Asteroid Tracking program at Palomar Observatory in California, United States. The asteroid was named for American astronaut and mission payload commander Mike Anderson, who died in the Space Shuttle Columbia disaster."@en .
