<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_181720> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "HD 181720 is an 8th-magnitude G-type main sequence star located approximately 190 light-years away in the constellation Sagittarius. This star is larger, hotter, brighter and less massive than our Sun. Also its metal content is three-tenths as much as the Sun. The star HD 181720 is named Sika. The name was selected in the NameExoWorlds campaign by Ghana, during the 100th anniversary of the IAU. Sika means gold in the Ewe language."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Weimar_Republic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/Place> .
