<http://dbpedia.org/resource/V_Persei> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "V Persei"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Alpha_Chamaeleontis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Place> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Alpha_Chamaeleontis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Alpha Chamaeleontis**, [Latinized](:Romanization_of_Greek) from α Chamaeleontis, is a solitary [star](:Star) in the southern [circumpolar constellation](:Circumpolar_constellation) of [Chamaeleon](:Chamaeleon). It has an [apparent visual magnitude](:Apparent_visual_magnitude) of 4.06 and thus is bright enough to be seen with the naked eye. With an annual [parallax shift](:Stellar_parallax) of 51.12 [mas](:Milliarcsecond), it is located 63.8 [light years](:Light_year) from the [Sun](:Sun). The star is drifting closer with a [radial velocity](:Radial_velocity) of −13 km/s, and is predicted to come to within 47 light-years in 666,000 years.This is an [F-type main sequence star](:F-type_main_sequence_star) with a [stellar classification](:Stellar_classification) of F5 V Fe−0.8, where the 'Fe−0.8' notation indicates an anomalously low abundance of [iron](:Iron). It has an estimated 1.4 times the [mass of the Sun](:Solar_mass), 2.1 times the [Sun's radius](:Sun%27s_radius), and radiates 7.5 times the [solar luminosity](:Solar_luminosity) from its [outer atmosphere](:Stellar_atmosphere) at an [effective temperature](:Effective_temperature) of 6,580 K. The star is around 1.8 billion years old with a [projected rotational velocity](:Projected_rotational_velocity) that is too low to be measured. The star has been examined for an [infrared excess](:Infrared_excess) that would suggest the presence of an orbiting [debris disk](:Debris_disk), but none was found."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
