<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_175289> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "HD 175289 is a binary star system. Its primary star, also known as Kepler-410A, is a F-type subgiant star, orbited by the orange dwarf star Kepler-410B on a wide orbit. The companion star was discovered in 2012. The primary star's surface temperature is 6325±75 K. HD 175289 is similar to the Sun in its concentration of heavy elements, with a metallicity Fe/H index of 0.01±0.10, but is much younger at an age of 1.81±0.27 billion years."@en .
