<http://dbpedia.org/resource/2201_Oljato> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**2201 Oljato**, provisional designation 1947 XC, is a stony and extremely eccentric [active](:Active_asteroid) [asteroid](:Asteroid) and sizable [near-Earth object](:Near-Earth_object) of the [Apollo group](:Apollo_asteroids), approximately 2 kilometers in diameter. It has an Earth [minimum orbit intersection distance](:Minimum_orbit_intersection_distance) of 0.0031 [AU](:Astronomical_unit) (460 thousand [km](:Kilometre%29) and is associated with the [Beta Taurids](:Beta_Taurids) daytime meteor shower."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
