<http://dbpedia.org/resource/BM_Andromedae> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**BM Andromedae** (**BM And**) is a [T Tauri star](:T_Tauri_star) in the [constellation](:Constellation) [Andromeda](:Andromeda_%28constellation%29). Its [apparent visual magnitude](:Apparent_visual_magnitude) has irregular variations between a maximum of 11.63 and a minimum of 14.02."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Markarian_177> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Markarian 177** is a [blue compact](:Dwarf_galaxy%23Blue_compact_dwarf_galaxies) [dwarf galaxy](:Dwarf_galaxy) located 90,000,000 ly (28 Mpc) away, at the [constellation](:Constellation) of [Ursa Major](:Ursa_Major), in the bowl of the [Big Dipper](:Big_Dipper) asterism. It was discovered by the astronomer [Benjamin Markarian](:Benjamin_Markarian).Markarian 177 is a [peculiar galaxy](:Peculiar_galaxy) that is receding from us at a rate of 2425 km/s. It has a visual apparent size of 0.41×0.34 [arcmin](:Arcmin)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Zeta_Tucanae> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/Star> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/3908_Nyx> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**3908 Nyx** is an [Amor](:Amor_asteroid) and [Mars-crosser asteroid](:Mars-crosser_asteroid). It was discovered by [Hans-Emil Schuster](:Hans-Emil_Schuster) on August 6, 1980, and is named after [Nyx](:Nyx_%28mythology%29), the [Greek](:Greek_mythology) goddess of the night, after which [Pluto](:Pluto)'s [moon](:Natural_satellite) [Nix](:Nix_%28moon%29) is also named. It is 1–2 km in diameter and is a [V-type asteroid](:V-type_asteroid), meaning that it may be a fragment of the asteroid [4 Vesta](:4_Vesta)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hamburg> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q515> .
