<http://dbpedia.org/resource/425_Cornelia> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/orbitalPeriod> "1,5466e+08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/IC_2233> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**IC 2233**, also known as **UGC 4278**, is a [spiral galaxy](:Spiral_galaxy) lying in the constellation of [Lynx](:Lynx_%28constellation%29). IC 2233 is located between 26 and 40 million light-years away from [Earth](:Earth). A comparatively quiet galaxy with a low rate of star formation (less than one solar mass every twenty years), it was long thought to be possibly interacting with the [Bear's Paw galaxy](:NGC_2537). However, this is now considered highly unlikely as [radio](:Radio_astronomy) observations with the [Very Large Array](:Karl_G%2E_Jansky_Very_Large_Array) showed the two galaxies lie at different distances. This galaxy was discovered by British astronomer [Isaac Roberts](:Isaac_Roberts) in 1894."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Annibale_de_Gasparis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q901> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_70930> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "HD 70930 is a binary star system in the southern constellation of Vela. It has the Bayer designation B Velorum, while HD 70930 is the star's identifier in the Henry Draper catalogue. With a combined apparent visual magnitude of 4.79, it is visible to the naked eye as a faint point of light. The distance to this system is approximately 1,700 light years based on parallax, and it has an absolute magnitude of −3.74. It is drifting further away from the Sun with a radial velocity of about +27 km/s. The system is a member of the Vel OB2 association of co-moving stars."@en .
