<http://dbpedia.org/resource/S/2004_S_12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "S/2004 S 12 is a natural satellite of Saturn. Its discovery was announced by Scott S. Sheppard, David C. Jewitt, Jan Kleyna, and Brian G. Marsden on May 4, 2005 from observations taken between December 12, 2004 and March 9, 2005. S/2004 S 12 is about 5 kilometres in diameter, and orbits Saturn at an average distance of 19.906 Gm in 1048.541 days, at an inclination of 164° to the ecliptic (162° to Saturn's equator), in a retrograde direction and with an eccentricity of 0.396. This moon was considered lost until its recovery in Canada-France-Hawaii Telescope observations from 2019."@en .
