<http://dbpedia.org/resource/10251_Mulisch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**10251 Mulisch**, provisional designation 3089 T-1, is a bright background [asteroid](:Asteroid) from the inner regions of the [asteroid belt](:Asteroid_belt), approximately 2.4 kilometers (1.5 miles) in diameter. It was discovered during the [Palomar–Leiden Trojan survey](:Palomar%E2%80%93Leiden_Trojan_survey) on 26 March 1971, by [Ingrid](:Ingrid_van_Houten-Groeneveld) and [Cornelis van Houten](:Cornelis_van_Houten) at Leiden, and [Tom Gehrels](:Tom_Gehrels) at [Palomar Observatory](:Palomar_Observatory) in California, United States. The asteroid was named after Dutch writer [Harry Mulisch](:Harry_Mulisch)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
