<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_72561> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "HD 72561 is a star in the constellation Hydra. Its apparent magnitude is 5.867. Based on parallax shift, it is located about 1,600 light-years (500 parsecs) away. HD 72561 is a G-type giant star. It is over 4 times as massive as the Sun and 48 times as wide. It is about 150 million years old."@en .
