<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mikko_Tuomi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Mikko Tuomi** is a Finnish astronomer from the [University of Hertfordshire](:University_of_Hertfordshire), most known for his contributions to the discovery of a number of [exoplanets](:Exoplanet), among them the [Proxima Centauri b](:Proxima_Centauri_b) which orbits the closest star to the Sun. Mikko Tuomi was the first to find indications of the existence of Proxima Centauri b in archival observation data. Other exoplanets to whose discovery or study Tuomi has contributed include [HD 40307](:HD_40307), [HD 154857 c](:HD_154857_c), [Kapteyn c](:Kapteyn_c), [Gliese 682 c](:Gliese_682_c), [HD 154857](:HD_154857), [Gliese 221](:Gliese_221), [Gliese 581 g](:Gliese_581_g) and the planetary system orbiting [Tau Ceti](:Tau_Ceti). He has led the development of new data analysis techniques for distinguishing observations caused by natural activity of the star and those caused by planets orbiting them."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
