<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Rho_Tauri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Rho Tauri (ρ Tau, ρ Tauri) is a star in the constellation Taurus and a member of the Hyades star cluster. Rho Tauri is a white A-type main sequence dwarf with a mean apparent magnitude of +4.66. It is approximately 158 light years from Earth. Classified as a Delta Scuti type variable star, its brightness varies by 0.010 magnitudes over a period of 1.61 hours. It has 1.88 times the mass of the Sun, with a projected rotational velocity of 117 km/s and an estimated rotation period of 488.5 days. \n* Hyades, with ρ Tau appearing blue, left of center, marked with a red arrow \n*"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/S_Normae> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**S Normae** (S Nor) is a [yellow supergiant](:Yellow_supergiant) [variable star](:Variable_star) in the [constellation](:Constellation) [Norma](:Norma_%28constellation%29). It is the brightest member of the [open cluster](:Open_cluster) [NGC 6087](:NGC_6087).S Normae is a [Classical Cepheid variable](:Classical_Cepheid_variable) with a visual magnitude range of 6.12 to 6.77 and a period of 9.75411 days. The spectral type varies during the pulsation cycle from F8 to G0. Its mass has been measured at 6.3 M☉ with reference to a close orbital companion, and it is over 3,000 times as luminous as the sun."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
