<http://dbpedia.org/resource/742_Edisona> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**742 Edisona** is a [minor planet](:Minor_planet) orbiting the [Sun](:Sun) that was discovered by German astronomer [Franz Kaiser](:Franz_Kaiser) on February 23, 1913. It was named for inventor [Thomas Edison](:Thomas_Edison). This asteroid is orbiting 3.01 [AU](:Astronomical_unit) with a [period](:Orbital_period) of 5.22 years and an [eccentricity](:Orbital_eccentricity) of 0.119. The [orbital plane](:Orbital_plane) is inclined at an angle of 11.2° to the [plane of the ecliptic](:Plane_of_the_ecliptic). This is a member of the dynamic [Eos family](:Eos_family) of asteroids that most likely formed as the result of a collisional breakup of a parent body.[Photometric](:Photometry_%28astronomy%29) observations made during 2008 were used to produce a [light curve](:Light_curve) of 742 Edisona showing a [rotation period](:Rotation_period) of 18.52±0.01 with a brightness variation of 0.30±0.01 in [magnitude](:Apparent_magnitude). It spans a girth of approximately 45.6 km."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
