<http://dbpedia.org/resource/1176_Lucidor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**1176 Lucidor**, provisional designation 1930 VE, is a carbonaceous background [asteroid](:Asteroid) from the central region of the [asteroid belt](:Asteroid_belt), approximately 30 kilometers in diameter. It was discovered by [Eugène Delporte](:Eug%C3%A8ne_Delporte) in 1930, who named it after a friend."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/TIC_168789840> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**TIC 168789840** is a [stellar system](:Stellar_system) with six stars. Three pairs of [binary stars](:Binary_star) circle a common [barycenter](:Barycenter). While other systems with three pairs of stars have been discovered, this was the first system where the stars can be observed [eclipsing](:Eclipse) one another, as their planes of rotation point approximately towards the [Earth](:Earth)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
