<http://dbpedia.org/resource/R_Serpentis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**R Serpentis** is a [Mira variable](:Mira_variable) type star in the [equatorial](:Celestial_equator) [constellation](:Constellation) of [Serpens](:Serpens). It ranges between apparent magnitude 5.16 and 14.4, and spectral types M5e to M8e, over a period of 356.41 days. The variability of this star was discovered in 1826 by [Karl Ludwig Harding](:Karl_Ludwig_Harding)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_154857> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**HD 154857** is a [star](:Star) with two [exoplanetary](:Exoplanet) companions in the southern [constellation](:Constellation) of [Ara](:Ara_%28constellation%29). It is too dim to be visible with the naked eye having an [apparent visual magnitude](:Apparent_visual_magnitude) of 7.25. The star is located at a distance of 207 [light years](:Light_year) from the [Sun](:Sun) based on [parallax](:Stellar_parallax) measurements, and is drifting further away with a [radial velocity](:Radial_velocity) of +28 km/s.This is a [G-type star](:G-type_star) with a [stellar classification](:Stellar_classification) of G5IV-V. The [absolute magnitude](:Absolute_magnitude) of this star is two magnitudes above the [main sequence](:Main_sequence), which suggests that the star is [evolving](:Stellar_evolution) toward the [subgiant](:Subgiant_star) stage. It is a [metal-poor](:Metallicity) [thin disk](:Thin_disk) star approximately six billion years old and is [chromopherically quiet](:Magnetic_activity) although not in a [Maunder Minimum](:Maunder_Minimum) state. The star is larger, more massive, and more luminous than the Sun. It is spinning with a [projected rotational velocity](:Projected_rotational_velocity) of 1.4 km/s."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
