<http://dbpedia.org/resource/99906_Uofalberta> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**99906 Uofalberta**, provisional designation 2002 QV53, is a dark background [asteroid](:Asteroid) from the outermost region of the [asteroid belt](:Asteroid_belt), approximately 6.8 kilometers (4.2 miles) in diameter. It was discovered by Canadian amateur astronomer [Andrew Lowe](:Andrew_Lowe) on 17 August 2002, from digitized photographic plates taken at the [Palomar Observatory](:Palomar_Observatory). It was named for the [University of Alberta](:University_of_Alberta)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
