<http://dbpedia.org/resource/51824_Mikeanderson> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**51824 Mikeanderson**, provisional designation 2001 OE30, is an Eoan [asteroid](:Asteroid) in the outer region of the [asteroid belt](:Asteroid_belt), approximately 5 kilometers in diameter. It was discovered on 19 July 2001, by astronomers of the [Near-Earth Asteroid Tracking](:Near-Earth_Asteroid_Tracking) program at [Palomar Observatory](:Palomar_Observatory) in [California](:California), [United States](:United_States). The asteroid was named for American astronaut and mission payload commander [Mike Anderson](:Michael_P%2E_Anderson), who died in the [Space Shuttle *Columbia* disaster](:Space_Shuttle_Columbia_disaster)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
