<http://dbpedia.org/resource/858_El_Djezaïr> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**858 El Djezaïr**  is a stony [asteroid](:Asteroid) from the [asteroid belt](:Asteroid_belt), about 24 kilometers in diameter. It was discovered on May 26, 1916, by French astronomer [Frédéric Sy](:Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Sy) at the [Algiers Observatory](:Algiers_Observatory) in Algeria, North Africa, and given the provisional designation 1916 a.The asteroid orbits the Sun at a distance of 2.5–3.1 [AU](:Astronomical_unit) once every 4.71 years (1,722 days). The bright [S-type asteroid](:S-type_asteroid) has a very high geometric albedo of 0.32. Its rotation period has been measured to take 22 hours and 20 minutes. Along with the asteroids [68 Leto](:68_Leto) and [236 Honoria](:236_Honoria), it is a member of the Leto family, a small, well-defined group of asteroids, all with a semi-major axis of close to 2.8 AU.El Djezaïr is the French spelling of the Arabic name for [Algiers](:Algiers), the capital of Algeria. It means \"the islands\". The asteroid was the first minor planet to receive a name that consists of more than one word. Its designation, 1916 a, is a superseded version of the modern two-letter code [system of provisional designation](:Provisional_designation_in_astronomy%23Minor_planets), implemented just a few years later in 1925."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
