<http://dbpedia.org/resource/456_Abnoba> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Abnoba (minor planet designation: 456 Abnoba), provisional designation 1900 FH, is a stony background asteroid from the central regions of the asteroid belt, approximately 40 kilometers in diameter. It was discovered on 4 June 1900, by astronomers Max Wolf and Arnold Schwassmann at the Heidelberg-Königstuhl State Observatory in southwest Germany. The asteroid was named after the Celtic deity Abnoba."@en .
