<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chi_Octantis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Chi Octantis**, [Latinized](:Romanization_of_Greek) from **χ Octantis**, is a solitary star in the southern [circumpolar constellation](:Circumpolar_constellation) [Octans](:Octans). It has an [apparent magnitude](:Apparent_magnitude) of 5.28, allowing it to be faintly seen with the [naked eye](:Naked_eye). Located 261 [light years](:Light_year) away, it is receding with a heliocentric [radial velocity](:Radial_velocity) 33.6 [km/s](:Metre_per_second).Chi Octantis is an [orange giant](:Orange_giant) with 125% the [mass of the Sun](:Mass_of_the_Sun) and an enlarged radius of 14.45 [*R*☉](:Solar_radius). It shines at 62.8 times the [luminosity of the Sun](:Luminosity_of_the_Sun) from its [photosphere](:Photosphere) at an [effective temperature](:Effective_temperature) of 4,266 [K](:Kelvin), giving it an orange glow. Chi Oct is metal enriched with an [iron](:Iron) abundance 126% that of the [Sun](:Sun) and spins slowly with a [projected rotational velocity](:Projected_rotational_velocity) less than 1 km/s−1."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
