<http://dbpedia.org/resource/CE_Gruis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "CE Gruis is a faint binary star system in the constellation Grus. It is a variable star, with a B-band brightness that ranges from a peak magnitude of 17.4 down to a minimum of 19.5 over a period of 108.6 minutes. The system is composed of a white dwarf and donor star, locked into a close, synchronous orbit. In such systems, known as polars, material from the donor star does not form an accretion disc around the white dwarf because of its intense magnetic field, but rather streams directly onto it along columns."@en .
