<http://dbpedia.org/resource/(11474)_1982_SM2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**(11474) 1982 SM2** is a carbonaceous Baptistina [asteroid](:Asteroid) and potentially [slow rotator](:List_of_slow_rotators_%28minor_planets%29) from the inner regions of the [asteroid belt](:Asteroid_belt), approximately 6 kilometers in diameter. It was discovered on 18 September 1982, by Belgian astronomer [Henri Debehogne](:Henri_Debehogne) at [ESO](:European_Southern_Observatory)' [La Silla Observatory](:La_Silla_Observatory) in northern Chile."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/NGC_484> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "NGC 484 is an elliptical galaxy in the constellation Tucana. It is located approximately 218 million light-years from Earth and was discovered on October 28, 1834 by astronomer John Herschel."@en .
