<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_72561> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**HD 72561** is a [star](:Star) in the [constellation](:Constellation) [Hydra](:Hydra_%28constellation%29). Its [apparent magnitude](:Apparent_magnitude) is 5.867. Based on [parallax shift](:Stellar_parallax), it is located about 1,600 light-years (500 parsecs) away.HD 72561 is a [G-type](:G-type_star) [giant star](:Giant_star). It is over 4 times as massive as the [Sun](:Sun) and 48 times as wide. It is about 150 million years old."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/BM_Andromedae> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "BM Andromedae (BM And) is a T Tauri star in the constellation Andromeda. Its apparent visual magnitude has irregular variations between a maximum of 11.63 and a minimum of 14.02."@en .
