<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eleanor_F._Helin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Eleanor Francis \"Glo\" Helin (née Francis, 19 November 1932 – 25 January 2009) was an American astronomer. She was principal investigator of the Near-Earth Asteroid Tracking (NEAT) program of NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory. (Some sources give her name as Eleanor Kay Helin.)"@en .
