<http://dbpedia.org/resource/861_Aïda> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**861 Aïda**  is a carbonaceous [asteroid](:Asteroid) from the outer region of the [asteroid belt](:Asteroid_belt), approximately 65 kilometers in diameter. It was discovered on 22 January 1917, by German astronomer [Max Wolf](:Max_Wolf) at [Heidelberg Observatory](:Heidelberg_Observatory) in southwest Germany, and given the provisional designation 1917 BE. It was named after the Italian opera [Aida](:Aida)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
