<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_156846> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**HD 156846** is a [binary star](:Binary_star) system in the [equatorial](:Celestial_equator) [constellation](:Constellation) of [Ophiuchus](:Ophiuchus), positioned a degree SSE of [Messier 9](:Messier_9). It has a yellow hue and is just barely bright enough to be visible to the naked eye with an [apparent visual magnitude](:Apparent_visual_magnitude) of 6.5. The system is located at a distance of 156 [light years](:Light_year) from the [Sun](:Sun) based on [parallax](:Stellar_parallax). It is drifting closer with a [radial velocity](:Radial_velocity) of −68.5 km/s, and is predicted to come to within 85.0 light-years in about 476,000 years.The primary, component A, is a [G-type star](:G-type_star) with a [stellar classification](:Stellar_classification) of G1V. The [absolute visual magnitude](:Absolute_visual_magnitude) of this star is 1.13 magnitudes above the [main sequence](:Main_sequence), indicating it has [evolved](:Stellar_evolution) slightly off the [main sequence](:Main_sequence). It has 1.35 times the [mass of the Sun](:Mass_of_the_Sun) and 2.12 times the [Sun's radius](:Sun%27s_radius). The star is an estimated 2.8 billion years old and is spinning with a [projected rotational velocity](:Projected_rotational_velocity) of 5 km/s. It is radiating five times the [luminosity of the Sun](:Luminosity_of_the_Sun) from its [photosphere](:Photosphere) at an [effective temperature](:Effective_temperature) of 5,969 K.The magnitude 14.4 secondary companion, component B, was discovered by the American astronomer [R. G. Aitken](:Robert_Grant_Aitken) in 1910. It lies at an [angular separation](:Angular_separation) of 5.1[″](:Second_of_arc) from the primary, corresponding to a [projected separation](:Projected_separation) of 250 [AU](:Astronomical_unit). This is a [red dwarf](:Red_dwarf) with a class of M4V and has an estimated 59% of the Sun's mass."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/6_Lyncis_b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**6 Lyncis b** (abbreviated **6 Lyn b**) is an [extrasolar planet](:Extrasolar_planet) orbiting the [K-type](:Stellar_classification%23Class_K) [subgiant](:Subgiant_star) [star](:Star) [6 Lyncis](:6_Lyncis) which is approximately 182 [light years](:Light_year) away in the [Lynx](:Lynx_%28constellation%29) [constellation](:Constellation). The planet has a [minimum mass](:Minimum_mass) 2.4 [MJ](:Jupiter_mass). The [orbital period](:Orbital_period) for this planet is 899 days, or 2.46 years. The [orbital radius](:Semimajor_axis) for this planet is 2.2 [AU](:Astronomical_unit), [periastron](:Periastron) 1.9 AU, and [apastron](:Apastron) 2.5 AU, corresponding to the [orbital eccentricity](:Orbital_eccentricity) of 0.134. This planet was discovered on July 3, 2008 by Sato *et al.*, who used [Doppler spectroscopy](:Doppler_spectroscopy) to find variations of the line of sight motion of the star caused by the planet’s gravity during its orbit."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
