<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_175289> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**HD 175289** is a binary star system. Its primary star, also known as Kepler-410A, is a F-type [subgiant star](:Subgiant_star), orbited by the [orange dwarf](:K-type_main-sequence_star) star Kepler-410B on a wide orbit. The companion star was discovered in 2012.The primary star's surface temperature is 6325±75 [K](:Kelvin). HD 175289 is similar to the [Sun](:Sun) in its concentration of heavy elements, with a [metallicity](:Metallicity) Fe/H index of 0.01±0.10, but is much younger at an age of 1.81±0.27 billion years."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
