<http://dbpedia.org/resource/456_Abnoba> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Abnoba** ([minor planet designation](:Minor_planet_designation): **456 Abnoba**), provisional designation 1900 FH, is a stony background [asteroid](:Asteroid) from the central regions of the [asteroid belt](:Asteroid_belt), approximately 40 kilometers in diameter. It was discovered on 4 June 1900, by astronomers [Max Wolf](:Max_Wolf) and [Arnold Schwassmann](:Arnold_Schwassmann) at the [Heidelberg-Königstuhl State Observatory](:Heidelberg-K%C3%B6nigstuhl_State_Observatory) in southwest Germany. The asteroid was named after the Celtic deity [Abnoba](:Abnoba)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
