<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_40307_e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "HD 40307 e is an extrasolar planet candidate suspected to be orbiting the star HD 40307. It is located 42 light-years away in the direction of the southern constellation Pictor. The planet was discovered by the radial velocity method, using the European Southern Observatory's HARPS apparatus by a team of astronomers led by Mikko Tuomi at the University of Hertfordshire and Guillem Anglada-Escude of the University of Göttingen, Germany. The existence of the planet was disputed in 2015, as more Doppler spectroscopy data has become available."@en .
