<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Zeta_Pavonis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Zeta Pavonis**, [Latinized](:Latinisation_of_names) from ζ Pavonis, is an orange-hued [star](:Star) in the southern [constellation](:Constellation) [Pavo](:Pavo_%28constellation%29). Its apparent magnitude is 4.01, which is bright enough to be faintly visible to the naked eye. The annual [parallax shift](:Stellar_parallax) of this star is 14.93 [mas](:Milliarcsecond) as seen from Earth, which provides a distance estimate of approximately 420 [light-years](:Light-year) (130 [parsecs](:Parsec%29) away from the Sun. It is moving closer to the Sun with a [radial velocity](:Radial_velocity) of −16.30. Based upon its motion through space, this star appears to be a member of the [Hyades Supercluster](:Hyades_Supercluster).This is an [evolved](:Stellar_evolution) [K-type](:K-type_star) [giant star](:Giant_star) with a [stellar classification](:Stellar_classification) of K0 III, which indicates it has exhausted the supply of hydrogen at its [core](:Stellar_core). The measured [angular diameter](:Angular_diameter) of this star, after correction for [limb darkening](:Limb_darkening), is 2.63±0.07 [mas](:Milliarcsecond). At the estimated distance of this star, this yields a physical size of about 19 times the [radius of the Sun](:Solar_radius). The star is radiating 155 times the [Sun's luminosity](:Sun%27s_luminosity).Zeta Pavonis has a companion, probably optical, of apparent magnitude 12.0 at about 55.6\" separation."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
