<http://dbpedia.org/resource/TIC_168789840> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "TIC 168789840 is a stellar system with six stars. Three pairs of binary stars circle a common barycenter. While other systems with three pairs of stars have been discovered, this was the first system where the stars can be observed eclipsing one another, as their planes of rotation point approximately towards the Earth."@en .
