<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Formation_and_evolution_of_the_Solar_System> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The formation of the Solar System began about 4.6 billion years ago with the gravitational collapse of a small part of a giant molecular cloud. Most of the collapsing mass collected in the center, forming the Sun, while the rest flattened into a protoplanetary disk out of which the planets, moons, asteroids, and other small Solar System bodies formed."@en .
