<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Phi_Aurigae> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Phi Aurigae**, [Latinized](:Latinisation_of_names) from φ Aurigae, is a [giant star](:Giant_star) in the northern [constellation](:Constellation) of [Auriga](:Auriga_%28constellation%29). It is faintly visible to the naked eye with an [apparent visual magnitude](:Apparent_visual_magnitude) of 5.089. It lies 10[′](:Minute_of_arc) from another faint naked-eye star [HD 35520](:HD_35520), between the three [open clusters](:Open_cluster) [M36](:Messier_36) and [M38](:Messier_38), and [NGC 1893](:NGC_1893).The distance to this star, as determined from [parallax](:Parallax) measurements, is approximately 480 [light-years](:Light-year) (150 [parsecs](:Parsec%29) with a 10 light-year [margin of error](:Margin_of_error). This is an [evolved](:Stellar_evolution) giant star with a [stellar classification](:Stellar_classification) of K3 IIIp and an estimated radius equal to 16 times the radius of the Sun. The [outer envelope](:Stellar_atmosphere) has an [effective temperature](:Effective_temperature) of 4,367 K, giving it the cool orange-hued glow of a [K-type star](:K-type_star)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
