<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nu1_Sagittarii> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Nu¹ Sagittarii (ν¹ Sagittarii, abbreviated Nu¹ Sgr, ν¹ Sgr) is a triple star system about 1,100 light-years from Earth. Its three components are designated Nu¹ Sagittarii A (officially named Ainalrami /ɛnəlˈreɪmi/, the traditional name for the system), B and C. A and B themselves form a spectroscopic binary. The system is 0.11 degree north of the ecliptic."@en .
