<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HD_181720> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**HD 181720** is an 8th-[magnitude](:Apparent_magnitude) [G-type](:G-type_star) [main sequence](:Main_sequence) [star](:Star) located approximately 190 [light-years](:Light-year) away in the [constellation](:Constellation) [Sagittarius](:Sagittarius_%28constellation%29). This star is larger, hotter, brighter and less massive than the [Sun](:Sun). Also its [metal](:Metallicity) content is three-tenths as much as the Sun.The star HD 181720 is named **Sika**. The name was selected in the [NameExoWorlds](:NameExoWorlds) campaign by [Ghana](:Ghana), during the 100th anniversary of the [IAU](:IAU). Sika means [gold](:Gold) in the [Ewe language](:Ewe_language)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
